---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const controller = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_PRIVACY_CONTROLLER;
const contact = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_PRIVACY_CONTACT_EMAIL;
---

<Base
  title="Privacy — CrowdCompute"
  description="How CrowdCompute handles expressions of interest and model votes."
>
  <article class="container privacy-page">
    <a class="text-link" href="/">
      ← Back to CrowdCompute
    </a>
    <span class="eyebrow">YOUR INFORMATION</span>
    <h1>Privacy, in plain language.</h1>
    <p class="large-copy">
      We collect a little information to find out whether this project should
      exist.
    </p>
    <p class="small muted">
      Last updated: 12 September 2026 · Consent version 2026-09-12
    </p>
    <h2>Who is behind this</h2>
    <p>
      CrowdCompute is an early-stage community AI compute initiative, not an
      operating AI service.
    </p>
    {controller ? (
      <p>
        The organiser responsible for this signup data is{' '}
        <strong>{controller}</strong>.
      </p>
    ) : (
      <p class="privacy-notice">
        The project organiser’s legal/controller identity must be added before
        public signups open. No company legal entity is asserted here.
      </p>
    )}
    {contact ? (
      <p>
        For privacy questions, access, corrections, deletion or withdrawing
        consent, contact <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a>.
      </p>
    ) : (
      <p class="privacy-notice">
        A monitored privacy contact must also be configured before collecting
        public submissions.
      </p>
    )}
    <p>
      Complete legal and controller information, together with the commercial
      service terms, will be provided before any commercial launch.
    </p>
    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your email address and country.</li>
      <li>Whether you would join at approximately €59/month.</li>
      <li>Your primary use case and model preference.</li>
      <li>Your optional comment, if you leave one.</li>
      <li>
        Your consent, its wording version, and submission/update timestamps.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The application does not store IP addresses, browser fingerprints, payment
      information or AI prompts and responses.
    </p>
    <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
    <p>
      We use this information to validate demand, understand intended uses,
      guide the community model choice and contact you about CrowdCompute’s
      launch. We rely on the consent you give when submitting the form. You can
      withdraw it.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not sell the collected information. We do not use advertising
      trackers, social tracking pixels or analytics cookies.
    </p>
    <h2>What is public</h2>
    <p>
      Only aggregate counts: total responses, the number answering “yes” at
      approximately €59/month, and totals for each model preference. No
      individual emails, countries, comments or votes are published. At very
      small sample sizes, totals may indirectly reveal preferences; avoid
      submitting sensitive information.
    </p>
    <h2>Storage and security checks</h2>
    <p>
      The site uses Cloudflare Pages, D1 and Turnstile. Cloudflare processes
      technical request information to deliver the site and protect it against
      abuse. This application does not copy that information into its signup
      database. Turnstile’s security checks involve Cloudflare processing
      technical browser data.
    </p>
    <p>
      A necessary, random browser receipt cookie (<code>cc_receipt</code>) lasts
      up to 180 days. It lets you update your existing response from the same
      browser without an account. Only its cryptographic hash is stored
      alongside your response. Losing the cookie means changes require
      contacting the organiser; knowing an email alone cannot change its vote.
    </p>
    <p>
      The intended European location of the future inference cluster is separate
      from this signup site’s hosting. A European-jurisdiction D1 database
      should be configured; Cloudflare’s global delivery and security services
      still process requests. See{' '}
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noreferrer">
        Cloudflare’s privacy policy
      </a>
      .
    </p>
    <h2>Retention and your choices</h2>
    <p>
      Signup records should be reviewed and deleted within 12 months of their
      last update, or sooner if the project is abandoned or you withdraw
      consent. The organiser must operate this retention process and handle
      deletion requests, including applicable backup retention. You may request
      access, correction or deletion using the privacy contact above.
    </p>
    <p>
      Where applicable, you may also contact your local data protection
      authority about how your data is handled.
    </p>
    <h2>No purchase. No service access yet.</h2>
    <p>
      This signup is an expression of interest only. It is not a binding
      purchase, does not give you ownership of any physical GPUs and does not
      give access to an AI service. No payments are collected.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
